From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:04:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 04/22] feat(qc): run the loudness and thought-boundary checks
 in the pipeline

The render stores the words around each clip's start and end in its
render-facts sidecar; TaskService._attach_render_facts sets the -14 LUFS
target and those words on ClipQcContext. Both checks stay warn-only and
never trigger a re-render. Off switches: CLIP_QC_LOUDNESS_LUFS=off,
CLIP_QC_THOUGHT_BOUNDARIES=0. test_clip_qc_pipeline turns loudness off:
its fixture clips are raw lavfi tones that never went through the
render's loudnorm=I=-14 step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
